 ## Overview
-Progressive Volume Distillation with Active Learning (PVD-AL) is a method for mutual conversion between different Neural Radiance Field (NeRF) architectures (implicit, explicit, and hybrid) [S1]. It accelerates distillation and improves synthesis quality by splitting the teacher and student models into cascaded modules and applying active learning strategies to select important camera poses, rays, and sample points [S1]. It sets itself apart from standard distillation by using a block-wise training schedule that avoids full network forward passes in early phases and by dynamically selecting hard examples across three levels of granularity [S1].
+Progressive Volume Distillation with Active Learning (PVD-AL) is a method for mutual conversion between different Neural Radiance Field (NeRF) architectures (implicit, explicit, and hybrid) [S1]. It accelerates distillation and improves synthesis quality by splitting the teacher and student models into cascaded modules and applying active learning strategies to select important camera poses, rays, and sample points [S1]. It sets itself apart from standard distillation by using a block-wise training schedule that spares networks from forwarding the entire network and rendering RGB outputs in early phases, and by dynamically selecting hard examples across three levels of granularity [S1].
 
